1
00:00:00,105 --> 00:00:02,645
Maybe it ends up being a film
about a director falling apart.

2
00:00:05,125 --> 00:00:05,965
No actors.

3
00:00:05,965 --> 00:00:07,425
Can’t find actors.

4
00:00:07,425 --> 00:00:08,825
Still wants to make the film.

5
00:00:08,825 --> 00:00:09,745
Falls apart.

6
00:00:09,745 --> 00:00:12,145
That is not impossible either.

7
00:00:12,145 --> 00:00:12,985
Anything is possible.

8
00:00:12,985 --> 00:00:13,985
I think that is good.

9
00:00:14,047 --> 00:00:15,658
It could become a different film.

10
00:00:15,658 --> 00:00:17,438
I would be pleasantly surprised.

11
00:00:18,998 --> 00:00:20,798
Impossible. Impossible.

12
00:00:21,038 --> 00:00:24,098
It is not impossible. That is
precisely what cinema makes
possible.

13
00:00:25,258 --> 00:00:26,478
The film could do that.

14
00:00:26,478 --> 00:00:28,878
Of course. That is what the film
could become.

15
00:00:28,898 --> 00:00:33,938
I have done so many performances
and never been short of male
actors.

16
00:00:33,938 --> 00:00:35,758
A surprise might do you good.

17
00:00:36,298 --> 00:00:38,238
No actors? I can accept that.

18
00:00:38,333 --> 00:00:40,693
What I mean is that I rather want
that absence.

19
00:00:40,693 --> 00:00:44,293
That absence could break your
reliance on many things.

20
00:00:44,394 --> 00:00:49,383
Possibility is not something you
can bring about by expecting it.
